{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (Task ID: 5270) to implement srd024-expand requirements R3.1-R3.4 (\"Exit codes and SIGPIPE\") in the existing `cmd/expand/main.go` file. The task requires:\n   - R3.1: Exit 0 when all inputs are processed successfully\n   - R3.2: Exit 1 when any input file cannot be opened, print error to stderr, continue processing remaining files\n   - R3.3: Exit 1 when a write error occurs on stdout\n   - R3.4: Handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n   \n   The user explicitly states: modify existing code, do not rewrite from scratch, preserve all existing R1.1-R2.4 functionality, do NOT run git commands.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` for differential testing against `gexpand`\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling\n   - `bufio.Writer` for buffered stdout writes with error accumulation\n   - Tab stop expansion with uniform intervals and absolute position lists\n   - Execution constitution: E8 (40-line function limit), E3 (no scope creep), E4 (no git commands)\n   - Go style constitution: copyright header, error handling with guard clauses, write-all-then-build strategy\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd024-expand.yaml**\n     - The SRD defining all requirements. R3 section (lines 42-52) specifies exit codes and SIGPIPE behavior.\n     - R3.1: Exit 0 on success\n     - R3.2: Exit 1 on file open error, print to stderr, continue processing\n     - R3.3: Exit 1 on stdout write error\n     - R3.4: SIGPIPE via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n\n   - **cmd/expand/main.go** (existing implementation, 158 lines)\n     - Already has `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at line 19 (R3.4)\n     - Already tracks `exitCode` initialized to 0 (R3.1) and sets to 1 on file open error (R3.2, lines 37-39)\n     - Has `w.Flush()` error check at lines 45-47 that exits 1 (partial R3.3)\n     - Key concern for R3.3: The `expand()` function (lines 122-145) calls `w.WriteByte()` without checking errors. While `bufio.Writer` accumulates errors internally for `Flush()`, write errors during processing are not detected immediately.\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd024-expand.\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"bufio\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"io\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strconv\"\n         \"strings\"\n     \n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         w := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n         stops, files, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         if err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"expand: %s\\n\", err)\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         exitCode := 0\n         if len(files) == 0 {\n             expand(os.Stdin, w, stops)\n         } else {\n             for _, name := range files {\n                 if name == \"-\" {\n                     expand(os.Stdin, w, stops)\n                     continue\n                 }\n                 f, err := os.Open(name)\n                 if err != nil {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"expand: %v\\n\", err)\n                     exitCode = 1\n                     continue\n                 }\n                 expand(f, w, stops)\n                 f.Close()\n             }\n         }\n         if err := w.Flush(); err != nil {\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         os.Exit(exitCode)\n     }\n     ```\n     - The `expand()` function:\n     ```go\n     func expand(r io.Reader, w *bufio.Writer, stops tabStops) {\n         br := bufio.NewReader(r)\n         col := 1\n         for {\n             b, err := br.ReadByte()\n             if err != nil {\n                 return\n             }\n             switch b {\n             case '\\t':\n                 spaces := nextTabSpaces(col, stops)\n                 for range spaces {\n                     w.WriteByte(' ')\n                 }\n                 col += spaces\n             case '\\n':\n                 w.WriteByte('\\n')\n                 col = 1\n             default:\n                 w.WriteByte(b)\n                 col++\n             }\n         }\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/expand/expand_test.go** (existing test file, 127 lines)\n     - Contains 23 differential test cases comparing against `gexpand`\n     - Covers default tab expansion, `-t N` uniform, `-t LIST` absolute positions, passthrough, multiple tabs, etc.\n     - Uses standard differential testing pattern with `testutils.BuildBinary` and `exec.LookPath(\"gexpand\")`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reading was completed before the summary request.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R3.1, R3.2, and R3.4 appear to be functionally present in the existing code already\n   - R3.3 (write error on stdout) is partially covered via the `w.Flush()` check, but the `expand()` function itself ignores `WriteByte` return values. Since `bufio.Writer` accumulates errors and reports them on `Flush()`, this is functionally sufficient but could be made more robust\n   - The main implementation work is to verify completeness and potentially strengthen write error handling in the `expand()` function\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - **Message 1**: Extremely long task description providing full project context, SRDs, constitutions, coding standards, and the specific task: implement srd024-expand R3.1-R3.4 in cmd/expand/main.go. Key quote: \"Add R3.1-R3.4 functionality to existing expand implementation\"\n   - **Message 2**: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — Instructing to provide a summary instead of continuing work.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Analyze whether the existing code fully satisfies R3.1-R3.4 or needs modifications\n   - If modifications needed, edit cmd/expand/main.go to strengthen write error handling (R3.3)\n   - Run `go build -o bin/expand ./cmd/expand/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/expand/...` to check for issues (AC2)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/expand/... -count=1` to verify differential tests pass\n   - Verify all four acceptance criteria (AC1-AC4)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just completed reading all three relevant files (the SRD, existing main.go, and existing test file) and was about to analyze the gap between existing code and R3.1-R3.4 requirements. The existing code at `cmd/expand/main.go` already has:\n   - SIGPIPE handler (R3.4) ✓\n   - Exit 0 on success (R3.1) ✓\n   - Exit 1 on file open error with stderr message (R3.2) ✓\n   - Flush error check exiting 1 (R3.3 partially) ✓\n   \n   The key question is whether R3.3 needs strengthening — specifically whether the `expand()` function should detect and propagate write errors rather than relying solely on `Flush()`. The `bufio.Writer` does accumulate errors, so `Flush()` will catch them, making the current implementation functionally correct. The task may simply require verifying this is adequate and running the acceptance criteria checks.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Determine if any code changes are needed for R3.1-R3.4 (the existing code appears to already implement them), then run `go build -o bin/expand ./cmd/expand/` and `go vet ./cmd/expand/...` and `go test ./cmd/expand/... -count=1` to verify acceptance criteria. The task description says: \"Implement srd024-expand requirement R3.1 as specified in the SRD\" through R